(There's also a version in G which has a little more lilt to it but is also played higher up, capo'd at the 5th fret.)

TIP:  For the intro, form the chord and then pick the note (which may or may not transpose).  Untransposed, it's hold (A); then pick the coverd 3rd string <a> and strum, then the covered 4th string <e> (or the open 6th string <e> if you prefer) and strum.  Repeat 3 times.

TIP:  The (D/A)s in the chorus can be ignored in favor of regular (D) without consequence but all you do is add your pinky to the 4th string/4th fret.


